WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.000 --> 00:03.700
(Episode 2)

3
00:05.710 --> 00:06.720
It's me.

4
00:08.790 --> 00:09.990
I'll be there soon.

5
02:32.100 --> 02:33.400
Three whole years.

6
02:35.410 --> 02:36.610
I'm finally back.

7
02:38.210 --> 02:39.510
Back in this living hell.

8
02:41.280 --> 02:46.030
Ow! But that was so cool, Kataoka-san!

9
02:49.890 --> 02:51.090
Cut! Cut!

10
02:54.030 --> 02:55.750
Sorry, I said what I was thinking out loud.

11
02:58.390 --> 02:59.390
Hey, Eiji.

12
02:59.680 --> 03:03.099
I was supposed to take down the pursuers and say, 'Like and subscribe!'

13
03:03.100 --> 03:05.760
- Wasn't that the plan? - Please, let's do one more take!

14
03:05.970 --> 03:06.820
Forget it.

15
03:06.821 --> 03:08.220
We're done filming. That's a wrap!

16
03:10.990 --> 03:12.090
More importantly,

17
03:17.010 --> 03:18.330
since we're finally back in town,

18
03:19.130 --> 03:20.259
let's grab a drink.

19
03:20.260 --> 03:21.950
Let's party hard!

20
04:29.600 --> 04:31.700
"The Journey To Killing You Season 2"

21
04:31.790 --> 04:33.039
Hey, listen up.

22
04:33.040 --> 04:35.590
A winning horse has an aura like no other.

23
04:36.120 --> 04:39.500
The moment our eyes met in the paddock, my gut knew that it was the one.

24
04:41.160 --> 04:44.019
From the gate, the two favorites fought for the lead.

25
04:44.020 --> 04:46.570
Meanwhile, my pick was dead last.

26
04:46.720 --> 04:50.700
Then, rounding the final turn, it started surging from the outside!

27
04:50.740 --> 04:53.370
Blazing down the final stretch with incredible speed!

28
04:53.540 --> 04:55.330
Can it pull through?

29
04:55.500 --> 04:56.569
Can it make it?!

30
04:56.570 --> 04:57.879
Will it pull through?

31
04:57.880 --> 04:58.880
Will it make it?!

32
05:01.840 --> 05:03.520
A stunning comeback win!

33
05:06.800 --> 05:08.600
Hey, you guys...

34
05:10.530 --> 05:12.020
Time for some pocket money!

35
05:15.850 --> 05:17.189
Go treat yourselves to whatever you like.

36
05:17.190 --> 05:18.540
My apologies.

37
05:19.230 --> 05:20.870
Hey, what do you feel like eating?

38
05:21.150 --> 05:23.020
- It's fine. - Sushi! Sushi! Sushi!

39
05:23.030 --> 05:25.150
He went completely wild at the track.

40
05:25.730 --> 05:26.930
I tried to stop him.

41
05:28.750 --> 05:30.280
Never mind. It's fine.

42
05:35.080 --> 05:36.080
So,

43
05:36.790 --> 05:38.630
the reason you called us here...

44
05:39.130 --> 05:40.810
What is this crisis facing the Kirii-gumi?

45
05:42.230 --> 05:43.230
Money.

46
05:45.550 --> 05:46.550
Six months ago,

47
05:48.110 --> 05:49.800
our parent organization, the Koutokukai,

48
05:50.010 --> 05:51.720
was taken over by the boss's son, Hanao.

49
05:51.930 --> 05:52.840
Huh?

50
05:52.850 --> 05:55.520
The head of the family isn't old enough to retire, is he?

51
05:56.270 --> 05:57.270
Did he die?

52
05:57.800 --> 05:58.800
No.

53
05:59.320 --> 06:01.590
Word is his twenty-seven-year-old new wife begged him,

54
06:02.450 --> 06:03.950
so he relocated to Cebu Island.

55
06:05.570 --> 06:07.130
That old man sure has plenty of energy.

56
06:08.663 --> 06:11.253
When it came to his son taking over the family,

57
06:12.030 --> 06:15.040
all the affiliates, including us, gave our approval.

58
06:15.580 --> 06:18.850
That should have been the end of it.

59
06:21.210 --> 06:22.210
Our dues...

60
06:23.590 --> 06:26.040
They raised our monthly tribute payment.

61
06:28.830 --> 06:29.830
Why the sudden hike?

62
06:31.970 --> 06:33.170
Awakuma...

63
06:33.550 --> 06:36.020
was selected for a massive urban redevelopment project.

64
06:36.730 --> 06:37.930
Awakuma?

65
06:38.710 --> 06:39.710
That's right.

66
06:40.230 --> 06:42.300
It's your old turf, Kataoka-san.

67
06:44.130 --> 06:45.610
They're redeveloping that place, huh?

68
06:45.940 --> 06:46.940
Yes.

69
06:47.610 --> 06:48.610
Because of that,

70
06:48.890 --> 06:50.840
claiming property values would surge,

71
06:51.470 --> 06:52.490
they jacked up the fee.

72
06:52.700 --> 06:56.280
Even with redevelopment, it takes years. How are you supposed to cash out right away?

73
06:56.400 --> 06:57.400
Exactly.

74
06:57.990 --> 06:58.990
On top of that,

75
07:00.290 --> 07:01.490
times are tough right now.

76
07:02.130 --> 07:04.690
Not only are relations with the locals in Awakuma deteriorating,

77
07:05.990 --> 07:08.060
our business operations are struggling.

78
07:09.010 --> 07:10.830
Were those locals always that difficult?

79
07:15.850 --> 07:19.260
If business is rough, just be straight with headquarters.

80
07:19.980 --> 07:21.830
We can't go against the parent family.

81
07:21.900 --> 07:24.500
- But weren't those two... - Under the previous boss,

82
07:25.650 --> 07:28.270
the parent family and our boss

83
07:29.110 --> 07:30.590
were certainly on good terms.

84
07:31.990 --> 07:32.990
However...

85
07:33.970 --> 07:35.170
the man calling the shots now,

86
07:36.290 --> 07:37.570
the President of the Koutokukai,

87
07:38.070 --> 07:39.170
Hikari Hanao,

88
07:39.990 --> 07:42.040
and Kirii Keito, head of the Kirii-gumi...

89
07:43.050 --> 07:44.206
The two of them are like oil and water.

90
07:44.230 --> 07:45.800
Things could explode at any moment.

91
07:48.610 --> 07:49.610
If they ever cross paths,

92
07:49.850 --> 07:51.290
an all-out turf war could break out.

93
07:58.010 --> 07:59.210
And there's nothing

94
07:59.670 --> 08:01.000
we can do about it.

95
08:05.030 --> 08:06.130
Please.

96
08:07.550 --> 08:08.650
Kataoka-san.

97
08:10.950 --> 08:12.150
At this rate,

98
08:13.690 --> 08:15.640
the Koutokukai will wipe us out completely.

99
08:19.770 --> 08:20.770
We beg of you.

100
08:23.810 --> 08:25.880
Please save the Kirii-gumi.

101
08:37.110 --> 08:38.440
Good work today.

102
08:41.750 --> 08:43.050
I'm back.

103
08:46.110 --> 08:47.110
Boss.

104
08:47.470 --> 08:49.000
Thank you for working so late.

105
08:52.950 --> 08:53.950
How did it go?

106
09:01.500 --> 09:05.670
I took over only to find the old man left behind a mountain of debt.

107
09:06.800 --> 09:10.920
Scraping by to pay it off while revenues keep shrinking...

108
09:11.000 --> 09:13.340
and now headquarters hikes our tribute.

109
09:16.830 --> 09:21.020
Even the bankers who milked us dry turned their backs on us.

110
09:24.590 --> 09:26.520
Crooked vultures. Worse than the yakuza.

111
09:28.980 --> 09:32.020
Boss, maybe we should...

112
09:32.670 --> 09:34.030
ask headquarters for an extension?

113
09:34.110 --> 09:36.900
I'd rather die than bow to them.

114
09:39.270 --> 09:40.510
Don't ever bring that up again.

115
09:59.530 --> 10:00.940
Smells awful in here.

116
10:04.430 --> 10:05.630
Did someone drop by?

117
10:06.240 --> 10:07.240
No.

118
10:19.850 --> 10:21.180
A mistress's place, huh?

119
10:22.350 --> 10:24.750
She went on a trip and said we could make ourselves at home?

120
10:26.090 --> 10:28.000
Old man Kumakura sure knows how to live.

121
10:30.650 --> 10:33.639
I get why I got called in.

122
10:33.640 --> 10:35.800
Still, making a move will have to wait until tomorrow.

123
10:42.650 --> 10:43.850
What?

124
10:44.570 --> 10:45.570
Nothing.

125
10:46.810 --> 10:49.120
You've been acting weird ever since we arrived.

126
10:49.750 --> 10:51.840
Are you mad because I was out having fun?

127
10:52.160 --> 10:52.798
I'm not mad.

128
10:52.822 --> 10:54.760
I won at the races, didn't I? What's the problem?

129
10:55.590 --> 10:56.590
Right.

130
10:57.690 --> 11:00.730
Odajima.

131
11:02.700 --> 11:03.700
I'm not mad.

132
11:04.670 --> 11:06.880
You haven't looked me in the eye once.

133
11:11.070 --> 11:12.070
Please take that off.

134
11:13.450 --> 11:15.340
You'll wrinkle the suit.

135
11:16.270 --> 11:17.400
Oh.

136
11:19.110 --> 11:21.070
We wore nothing but Hawaiian shirts on the island.

137
11:21.353 --> 11:23.713
Putting on a suit after so long makes me look pretty sharp.

138
11:28.710 --> 11:29.710
Hm?

139
11:31.190 --> 11:32.190
Ah...

140
11:33.030 --> 11:34.230
So that's what it is.

141
11:36.190 --> 11:37.390
Could it be...

142
11:38.950 --> 11:40.980
seeing me in a suit got you flustered?

143
11:45.780 --> 11:46.980
I am not flustered.

144
11:48.130 --> 11:49.500
- I'll run the bath. - Okay.

145
11:50.230 --> 11:51.420
Make it piping hot.

146
11:51.670 --> 11:53.270
My grandfather was old-school Edo.

147
11:53.500 --> 11:55.300
If the bath isn't scalding, it doesn't count.

148
11:55.380 --> 11:56.550
That's a family rule.

149
11:56.590 --> 11:57.600
A family rule.

150
11:57.670 --> 11:58.670
I know.

151
12:13.710 --> 12:14.710
Odajima.

152
12:15.730 --> 12:17.030
It's Kataoka-san.

153
12:17.590 --> 12:18.980
So handsome.

154
12:27.620 --> 12:31.710
The water temperature is set to forty-two degrees.

155
12:36.380 --> 12:37.390
Good.

156
12:38.210 --> 12:39.210
Let's head out.

157
12:50.290 --> 12:51.840
Just as I thought.

158
13:09.810 --> 13:10.810
Kataoka...

159
13:16.550 --> 13:18.380
That look on your face...

160
13:20.510 --> 13:21.510
It's magnificent.

161
14:18.760 --> 14:19.760
Excuse me.

162
14:23.530 --> 14:25.420
Word is Kataoka's back.

163
14:26.730 --> 14:27.730
Kataoka?

164
14:28.650 --> 14:29.850
Didn't he leave the syndicate

165
14:30.190 --> 14:31.680
to play house with his little hubby?

166
14:50.170 --> 14:51.720
Good for him.

167
14:53.370 --> 14:54.670
He went legit,

168
14:55.130 --> 14:57.920
and now he's meddling in yakuza affairs again?

169
15:00.030 --> 15:02.060
I love that shameless audacity.

170
15:13.090 --> 15:14.090
Good morning!

171
15:15.040 --> 15:17.820
- Huh? - Boss Kumakura sent me to drive for you!

172
15:17.990 --> 15:19.330
I'm Kazuki!

173
15:20.490 --> 15:21.690
- Please, get in! - All right.

174
15:22.330 --> 15:24.210
- You're full of energy, aren't you? - Yes, sir!

175
15:26.910 --> 15:27.910
Right this way!

176
15:33.117 --> 15:33.918
(Odajima and the boss are back. Pick them up here tomorrow at 10:00.

177
15:33.942 --> 15:34.786
Don't ask questions. Just follow Kataoka's orders.)

178
15:34.810 --> 15:36.746
(Understood! I've already met up with Kataoka-san and Odajima-san!)

179
15:36.770 --> 15:40.020
Four generations of pride, and look what we've become.

180
15:43.710 --> 15:44.710
Boss...

181
15:45.170 --> 15:47.130
Maybe we should talk to headquarters after all...

182
15:48.910 --> 15:50.240
Don't make me repeat myself.

183
15:51.010 --> 15:52.730
How many years have you been in the yakuza?

184
15:54.010 --> 15:55.620
Our pride is our life.

185
15:56.970 --> 15:59.770
Even for a boss, show a hint of weakness and they'll devour you alive.

186
16:09.570 --> 16:10.980
Especially that bastard.

187
16:14.470 --> 16:15.470
Kid.

188
16:15.910 --> 16:17.880
- Take us here. - Yes, sir!

189
16:22.170 --> 16:23.170
Hm?

190
16:24.100 --> 16:25.250
Thank you very much!

191
16:28.330 --> 16:31.060
Is the AC too cold or too warm?

192
16:31.070 --> 16:32.950
It's fine. Just right.

193
16:40.350 --> 16:43.050
- Something on your mind, kid? - N-No, nothing!

194
16:44.290 --> 16:45.730
Speak up if you need to take a dump.

195
16:46.000 --> 16:47.290
N-No, it's not that...

196
16:52.400 --> 16:54.510
Better spit it out before he loses his temper.

197
16:54.760 --> 16:58.610
Boss Kumakura told me to keep my mouth shut and just drive, but...

198
17:02.600 --> 17:04.729
Ah, I can't hold it in anymore!

199
17:04.730 --> 17:06.100
I just have to say it!

200
17:06.520 --> 17:09.370
I'm Kataoka-san's biggest fan!

201
17:12.230 --> 17:13.760
Hey, did you hear that, Odajima?

202
17:14.490 --> 17:15.490
I've still got it.

203
17:16.630 --> 17:17.630
Sure.

204
17:18.670 --> 17:19.670
And also...

205
17:19.740 --> 17:21.750
Odajima-san, I'm a huge fan of yours too!

206
17:21.860 --> 17:22.860
Huh?

207
17:23.700 --> 17:25.000
Of course I follow...

208
17:26.350 --> 17:27.860
'KinRen'!

209
17:29.490 --> 17:31.419
KinRen?

210
17:31.536 --> 17:33.005
Two hundred thousand followers!

211
17:33.030 --> 17:34.920
This is insane!

212
17:35.116 --> 17:38.086
I can't believe I'm driving for KinRen!

213
17:38.730 --> 17:39.730
Keep it down, will you?

214
17:40.370 --> 17:41.390
Is this...

215
17:41.850 --> 17:43.360
Looking good! Very nice.

216
17:48.590 --> 17:50.060
Hey, Odajima, dance a little more.

217
17:50.400 --> 17:51.400
Okay.

218
17:54.370 --> 17:56.599
Yes, yes, yes!

219
17:56.600 --> 17:57.600
Awesome.

220
17:58.690 --> 17:59.840
Looking good.

221
18:01.660 --> 18:03.059
Did you publish that video?

222
18:03.060 --> 18:04.096
The whole world can see it.

223
18:04.120 --> 18:05.500
I even monetized it.

224
18:06.810 --> 18:07.979
By the way,

225
18:07.980 --> 18:09.730
why is it called 'KinRen'?

226
18:10.290 --> 18:12.400
Because I'm Kinji, and he's Ren.

227
18:13.570 --> 18:14.970
Ah, makes sense.

228
18:17.530 --> 18:19.260
- Time to roll. - Yeah.

229
18:55.800 --> 18:57.120
There's two hundred million here.

230
18:57.300 --> 18:58.500
I'm leaving the syndicate.

231
19:00.160 --> 19:01.460
It's all yours.

232
19:25.220 --> 19:26.690
- Thanks. - Yes, sir!

233
19:27.860 --> 19:29.270
What kind of place is this?

234
19:30.040 --> 19:31.040
A diner.

235
19:31.120 --> 19:32.580
It's ridiculously run-down.

236
19:32.960 --> 19:34.460
You sure don't hold back, do you?

237
19:34.840 --> 19:35.840
I'm Kazuki!

238
19:38.800 --> 19:40.510
Go grab a coffee somewhere nearby.

239
19:40.740 --> 19:41.740
Whoa!

240
19:42.300 --> 19:43.300
Thank you so much!

241
19:43.930 --> 19:45.230
- Let's go. - Right.

242
19:51.680 --> 19:52.680
Yo.

243
19:55.240 --> 19:56.540
Haven't seen you around.

244
19:57.620 --> 19:59.410
I don't waste my breath on punks.

245
19:59.820 --> 20:00.820
Get lost.

246
20:15.060 --> 20:16.800
Don't be an idiot.

247
20:17.090 --> 20:19.770
Forget breasts, it's all about the ass!

248
20:19.840 --> 20:22.380
Right? A tight one, especially.

249
20:23.300 --> 20:26.010
See, you get it! Ass reigns supreme.

250
20:26.140 --> 20:29.680
My wife might be flat-chested, but that ass is out of this world.

251
20:30.390 --> 20:31.786
And this right here is my lovely wife.

252
20:31.810 --> 20:33.010
Kataoka-san...

253
20:42.120 --> 20:43.120
I see.

254
20:44.500 --> 20:46.090
So you're Kataoka.

255
20:49.660 --> 20:51.580
You're looking more like your old man every day.

256
20:55.200 --> 20:56.200
Yeah?

257
20:56.660 --> 20:58.100
Do I really look that much like him?

258
21:04.400 --> 21:05.520
What you came here to dig up

259
21:05.920 --> 21:07.500
is intel on the Koutokukai, right?

260
21:14.740 --> 21:16.010
They're dangerous.

261
21:17.580 --> 21:19.630
Hanao took over as boss six months ago,

262
21:21.020 --> 21:22.870
and he completely ditched the old ways.

263
21:23.360 --> 21:24.960
He overhauled how they make their money.

264
21:27.640 --> 21:29.650
To get what he wants,

265
21:30.860 --> 21:32.060
he stops at nothing.

266
21:34.740 --> 21:38.050
He poached an executive named Ihashi from another crew

267
21:39.320 --> 21:41.030
to be his right-hand man,

268
21:41.280 --> 21:42.690
running the syndicate's finances.

269
21:45.880 --> 21:47.730
Now the cash is multiplying,

270
21:48.780 --> 21:50.390
and their power is skyrocketing.

271
21:51.740 --> 21:53.430
Like a monstrous beast.

272
21:54.980 --> 21:56.180
A beast, huh?

273
22:09.680 --> 22:12.170
Word is the Koutokukai's next prey

274
22:13.480 --> 22:16.510
is Awakuma, right before redevelopment begins.

275
22:17.780 --> 22:19.080
Awakuma...

276
22:20.260 --> 22:24.549
A billion brought in from illegal casinos. Seven hundred million from the waste management bid.

277
22:24.550 --> 22:26.510
Eighty million in tribute from branch families...

278
22:28.580 --> 22:30.890
No matter how many designer bags I send,

279
22:31.200 --> 22:33.810
those women in Ginza keep sending them back.

280
22:34.540 --> 22:36.250
Why aren't I popular?

281
22:40.086 --> 22:42.216
I'm such a high-quality man.

282
22:44.690 --> 22:46.500
What do you think, Ihashi?

283
22:47.080 --> 22:49.569
My looks and personality are top-tier.

284
22:49.570 --> 22:50.720
Not to mention,

285
22:50.940 --> 22:52.040
I'm loaded.

286
22:53.780 --> 22:55.569
That lies outside my area of expertise.

287
22:55.570 --> 22:56.780
I wouldn't know.

288
23:02.300 --> 23:04.020
Speaking of which, that underling of yours.

289
23:04.860 --> 23:06.250
How dare he cook the books?

290
23:10.100 --> 23:12.750
After I sliced off four of his fingers,

291
23:13.740 --> 23:14.820
he confessed to everything.

292
23:17.380 --> 23:19.490
Claimed he acted entirely alone.

293
23:22.800 --> 23:25.030
He still had six left. Spineless coward.

294
23:29.360 --> 23:31.350
I take full responsibility. My apologies.

295
23:32.400 --> 23:33.400
Hey.

296
23:33.920 --> 23:36.390
Modern incinerators are truly impressive.

297
23:37.740 --> 23:40.130
They dispose of a corpse without leaving a trace of bone.

298
23:41.380 --> 23:43.910
The remaining ash gets mixed into concrete

299
23:44.760 --> 23:46.390
to form the foundations of skyscrapers.

300
23:51.300 --> 23:52.870
Regarding your earlier question...

301
23:53.420 --> 23:56.500
I believe no woman would fall for a man whose heart already belongs elsewhere.

302
23:56.970 --> 23:57.970
Belongs elsewhere?

303
24:01.350 --> 24:02.350
Ah.

304
24:03.620 --> 24:04.920
You're right.

305
24:14.680 --> 24:16.570
My one true love is this city.

306
24:18.700 --> 24:20.570
I will possess it all.

307
24:22.240 --> 24:23.790
And anyone who stands in my way...

308
24:25.540 --> 24:26.810
I'll slaughter them.

309
24:28.420 --> 24:29.420
Mister.

310
24:30.200 --> 24:31.200
Hey, mister...

311
24:33.250 --> 24:34.250
He's fast asleep.

312
24:35.760 --> 24:37.800
Hey, you'll catch a cold sleeping there, old-timer.

313
24:45.640 --> 24:47.370
He said I look more like my old man.

314
24:48.400 --> 24:49.880
Not that I have many memories of him.

315
24:51.200 --> 24:53.070
I think it was during a turf war...

316
24:54.760 --> 24:55.960
Killed in action.

317
25:08.320 --> 25:09.320
All right.

318
25:09.940 --> 25:10.940
Let's head out.

319
25:12.240 --> 25:13.440
Where are we going?

320
25:13.900 --> 25:15.370
Where else? Obviously...

321
25:16.560 --> 25:18.050
The Koutokukai headquarters.

322
25:18.900 --> 25:20.140
To pay their president a visit.

323
25:23.540 --> 25:24.690
Thanks for the meal.

324
25:24.730 --> 25:25.730
Please get in!

325
25:25.980 --> 25:27.020
No need for the car.

326
25:27.110 --> 25:28.490
- Huh? - We'll walk.

327
25:29.840 --> 25:31.280
It's right around the corner anyway.

328
25:31.820 --> 25:33.870
Then I'll park and catch up right away!

329
25:34.400 --> 25:36.310
- Kataoka-san. - Yeah?

330
25:37.110 --> 25:38.110
Kataoka-san!

331
25:38.140 --> 25:39.556
Storming headquarters like this is reckless!

332
25:39.580 --> 25:42.160
Storming? Don't make it sound so violent.

333
25:42.760 --> 25:44.436
We're just dropping by to talk. A friendly chat.

334
25:44.460 --> 25:45.000
Still...

335
25:45.040 --> 25:47.500
We left the syndicate. We're civilians now.

336
25:47.540 --> 25:48.990
That excuse won't protect us.

337
25:49.740 --> 25:51.070
You worry too much.

338
25:57.160 --> 25:58.800
What will you do if they take me hostage?

339
26:09.190 --> 26:10.750
Kataoka-san!

340
26:13.860 --> 26:14.910
I won't let that happen.

341
26:16.320 --> 26:18.120
This time, I will protect you no matter what.

342
26:19.620 --> 26:21.130
In life and death, we stick together.

343
26:26.160 --> 26:28.160
Come to think of it, I don't think I ever told you

344
26:28.820 --> 26:30.750
the reason I married you in the first place.

345
26:35.060 --> 26:36.590
I'll tell you when we get back.

346
26:38.380 --> 26:39.380
Ren.

347
26:54.230 --> 26:55.740
Odajima!

348
27:03.990 --> 27:05.869
Renren... I mean,

349
27:05.870 --> 27:08.280
Odajima-san, are you all right?!

350
27:08.670 --> 27:09.710
- After them! - But...

351
27:09.790 --> 27:11.410
- Go, now! - Yes, sir!

352
27:26.680 --> 27:27.900
(Next Episode Preview)

353
27:27.940 --> 27:28.940
You guys...

354
27:29.380 --> 27:30.980
Were you being targeted from the start?!

355
27:31.560 --> 27:33.626
Around here, the only crew reckless enough to pull off a kidnapping

356
27:33.650 --> 27:35.110
is VOID.

357
27:35.400 --> 27:36.820
If we make one wrong move,

358
27:36.990 --> 27:39.600
Kataoka-san might never come back.

359
27:40.440 --> 27:41.280
What do you want from me?

360
27:41.370 --> 27:43.130
Are you telling me to beg that guy for help?

361
27:43.160 --> 27:44.410
That guy...

362
27:44.790 --> 27:47.230
- He's out of control again, isn't he? - Where is Kataoka-san?

363
27:47.910 --> 27:49.050
Don't push your luck.

364
27:49.160 --> 27:50.240
Odajima.

365
27:51.040 --> 27:52.040
This is bad.

366
27:52.860 --> 27:54.360
It's all

367
27:54.720 --> 27:56.270
under my control.
